Part 2: Additional Notices for the Open Source Stock Screener
These notices apply to everyone who downloads, installs, copies, modifies, or uses the Software. To the extent they conflict with the MIT License in Part 1, Part 1 prevails.

1. What the Software Is
“Software” means the FinHavenArc Screener, including the files RSI_search.py, scheduler.py, markets.py, watchlists.py, and check_watchlists.py, and its documentation. The file secrets.env is not part of the Software. You create it yourself, and it contains your own Telegram bot token. Your own chat ID is entered in RSI_search.py.

2. You Are Responsible for What You Run
The Software is open source, and you are free to change it, extend it, combine it with other code, and run it however you like. That freedom comes with responsibility. You alone are responsible for the Software as you install, configure, modify, and operate it, and for any consequences. This includes any change made by you or by anyone from whom you obtained a modified copy. As an extreme example, if you or anyone else adds a command such as format c: to the code and it erases your data, the Licensor is not responsible for that loss. The same applies to every bug, error, malfunction, or unexpected behavior of the Software, whether it existed in the original code or came from a change.

3. No Financial Advice
The Software is an information tool. It applies fixed mechanical rules to market data. Nothing that the Software produces, and nothing in its documentation, is investment, financial, legal, or tax advice, a recommendation, an offer, or a solicitation to buy or sell any security or other instrument. The Software does not know your circumstances, goals, or risk tolerance. The rules have not been proven by backtesting, and no outcome or profit is promised. Trading and investing involve a risk of loss, including the loss of all of the money invested. All decisions are yours alone, and you should verify prices, conditions, and alerts independently before you act.

4. Data and Alerts May Be Wrong
The Licensor gives no guarantee that market data is timely, complete, or accurate, or that any alert will be generated, correct, on time, free of duplicates, or delivered. Free data can arrive late, can be missing or wrong, and can become unavailable or blocked at any time. Servers, networks, schedulers, and third-party services can fail or change without notice, and the Software may stop working after such changes.

5. Third-Party Services and Libraries
The Software works together with third-party libraries (including yfinance, pandas, NumPy, requests, exchange_calendars, and tzdata) and retrieves market data from Yahoo Finance through the independent yfinance library. It sends messages through Telegram. These libraries and services are not part of the Software, each is governed by its own license or terms, and the Licensor is not affiliated with Yahoo, Telegram, any exchange, any broker, or the authors of those libraries. The MIT License covers only the Software’s own code. It grants no rights to any third-party data or service. You alone are responsible for using them in line with their terms and applicable law. The terms of Yahoo Finance generally allow the free use of its data for personal, non-commercial purposes only, so check them before using the Software for any other purpose. These services can change, limit, or end access at any time.

6. Credentials and Privacy
The Software contains no telemetry and sends no data to the Licensor. It runs on your own infrastructure and communicates only with Yahoo Finance and Telegram (and, when you install or update packages, with package servers). You are responsible for keeping your Telegram bot token, chat ID, API keys, and secrets.env private. Never publish or share them, and do not include them if you pass on a copy of the Software. For how personal information is handled on the Website, see the Privacy Policy.

7. Support and Updates
The Licensor offers free, best-effort support for questions about installing, setting up, and using the Software, with no service level, guaranteed response time, or obligation to continue. Custom work, such as changing the filtering logic, selecting instruments by other criteria, or installing and administering servers, is outside the free support and may be offered for a fee under a separate written agreement. The Licensor has no obligation to provide updates, fixes, new versions, or updated ticker lists. Any review or update that the documentation mentions is only a possibility, not a promise.

